{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600172",
      "title": "Redux with Class-based Components",
      "sourceHash": "80a9c96c302838b423bca2123e9e7fc00c2484e1b82d9c5d8c4f9eacd308d11e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 3.15,
          "en": "Now, even though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.15,
          "end": 5.33,
          "en": "it's not the focus of this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.33,
          "end": 8.83,
          "en": "because it's not the common way of writing components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.83,
          "end": 12.92,
          "en": "I wanna briefly talk about class-based components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.92,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "instead of functional components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 17.36,
          "en": "Because whilst nowadays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.36,
          "end": 21.02,
          "en": "we typically do use functional components only,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.02,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "there still are a lot of projects out there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 26.97,
          "en": "that do use class-based components instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.97,
          "end": 30.05,
          "en": "And there of course also are simply people who prefer that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.05,
          "end": 33.8,
          "en": "and there is nothing wrong with class-based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.8,
          "end": 35.41,
          "en": "Therefore, I also wanna show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.41,
          "end": 38.43,
          "en": "how this counter component would look like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 41.403,
          "en": "if we would build it as a class-based component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.38,
          "end": 46.69,
          "en": "For this, I'll add a class named counter here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.69,
          "end": 51.69,
          "en": "and that class needs to extend the react component object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.15,
          "end": 55.33,
          "en": "the react component class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.33,
          "end": 60.33,
          "en": "So I'll import from react, I will import components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.42,
          "end": 64.82,
          "en": "whoops, component like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.82,
          "end": 68.76,
          "en": "And with that imported here we extend component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.76,
          "end": 69.83,
          "en": "Now, that's what you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.83,
          "end": 72.92,
          "en": "in a separate module about class-based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.92,
          "end": 74.083,
          "en": "That's how they work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.12,
          "end": 78.21000000000001,
          "en": "Now, in here, we then can add a constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.21000000000001,
          "end": 83,
          "en": "to initialize our state, but here we don't have any state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83,
          "end": 86.2,
          "en": "Instead here, we then add the render method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.2,
          "end": 89.06,
          "en": "which should of course return this JS X code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.06,
          "end": 92.733,
          "en": "So I'll copy that and return this JS X code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.75,
          "end": 95.47999999999999,
          "en": "But now we need to add increment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.47999999999999,
          "end": 97.66,
          "en": "and decrement handler methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.66,
          "end": 99.53999999999999,
          "en": "a toggle counter handler method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.53999999999999,
          "end": 102,
          "en": "even though we're not doing anything with that yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 103.44,
          "en": "And we then need to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.44,
          "end": 105.663,
          "en": "that we get access to our counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.93,
          "end": 109.24000000000001,
          "en": "So let's add a couple of methods here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.24000000000001,
          "end": 112.56,
          "en": "Let's start with the increment handler method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.56,
          "end": 115.02000000000001,
          "en": "then the decrement handler method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.02000000000001,
          "end": 117.523,
          "en": "and also the toggle counter handler method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.53999999999999,
          "end": 122.393,
          "en": "And this is how we can add methods in JavaScript classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 128.47,
          "en": "Now, down here, we now wanna hook this up correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.47,
          "end": 130.55,
          "en": "by using this increment handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.55,
          "end": 134.76,
          "en": "and this decrement handler and this toggle counter handler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.76,
          "end": 138.8,
          "en": "referring to these methods, which are part of this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.8,
          "end": 141.1,
          "en": "And then the question now is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.1,
          "end": 144.44,
          "en": "how do we get access to Redux here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.44,
          "end": 147.28,
          "en": "In the functional component we used hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.28,
          "end": 149.82999999999998,
          "en": "Use dispatch and use selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.82999999999998,
          "end": 153.433,
          "en": "but hooks are not usable in class-based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.42000000000002,
          "end": 156.91,
          "en": "Now, I briefly did mention it before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.91,
          "end": 161.04,
          "en": "react Redux also exports a connect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.04,
          "end": 163.39,
          "en": "which is a function that helps you connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.39,
          "end": 166.81,
          "en": "class-based components to Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.81,
          "end": 170.35,
          "en": "Actually, you could also use it on functional components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.35,
          "end": 173.53,
          "en": "but for functional components, using these hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.53,
          "end": 176.13,
          "en": "is simply more convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.13,
          "end": 177.87,
          "en": "But no matter if it's a functional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.87,
          "end": 181,
          "en": "or a class-based component, you can use connect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181,
          "end": 182.74,
          "en": "And therefore we will use connect here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.74,
          "end": 185.32,
          "en": "on this class-based component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.32,
          "end": 186.96,
          "en": "How do we use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.96,
          "end": 189.25,
          "en": "When we export our counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.25,
          "end": 192.67,
          "en": "we don't export the counter component like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.67,
          "end": 197.55,
          "en": "Instead we call connect and now connect when executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.55,
          "end": 201.61,
          "en": "will actually return a new function as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.61,
          "end": 204.9,
          "en": "which we then execute again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204.9,
          "end": 207.25,
          "en": "And then we pass our component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.25,
          "end": 210.803,
          "en": "to that returned function as our argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.67000000000002,
          "end": 213.18,
          "en": "So this can look strange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.18,
          "end": 216.61,
          "en": "but connect is a so-called higher order component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.61,
          "end": 219.01,
          "en": "We execute the connect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.01,
          "end": 221.69,
          "en": "It then returns a new function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.69,
          "end": 226.51,
          "en": "and we execute this returned, this new function as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.51,
          "end": 230.05,
          "en": "And to this returned function, we pass counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.05,
          "end": 232.32999999999998,
          "en": "Now, why do we do it like this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.32999999999998,
          "end": 235.69,
          "en": "Because to connect, when we execute this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.69,
          "end": 238.04,
          "en": "we also pass something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.04,
          "end": 241.88,
          "en": "Connect also wants some arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.88,
          "end": 245,
          "en": "Connect also wants some arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245,
          "end": 247.66,
          "en": "It wants two arguments to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.66,
          "end": 250.7,
          "en": "and both arguments are functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 250.7,
          "end": 252.61,
          "en": "I'll write them separately here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.61,
          "end": 257.28,
          "en": "The first function is a function that maps Redux state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.28,
          "end": 261.62,
          "en": "to props, which will be received in this component then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.62,
          "end": 266.03,
          "en": "Hence we call this function map state to props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 266.03,
          "end": 267.75,
          "en": "That's not a name you must use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 267.75,
          "end": 271.58,
          "en": "but a convention which you will see in a lot of projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 271.58,
          "end": 274.9,
          "en": "Now, this is a function which receives the Redux state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 274.9,
          "end": 279.48,
          "en": "and then this returns an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 279.48,
          "end": 281.94,
          "en": "where the keys will be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.94,
          "end": 284.65,
          "en": "as props in the receiving component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.65,
          "end": 288.53,
          "en": "So in the counter component, and the values of those keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.53,
          "end": 293.01,
          "en": "that is then the logic for drilling into that Redux state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.01,
          "end": 298.01,
          "en": "So here we could expose a counter prop by using counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 298.28,
          "end": 301.94,
          "en": "as a key here, this key named therefore is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.94,
          "end": 305.25,
          "en": "And the value is state.counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 305.25,
          "end": 308.58,
          "en": "So we then pick the counter value from the Redux state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 308.58,
          "end": 312.03,
          "en": "and bind that value to the counter prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.03,
          "end": 314.316,
          "en": "That's what we do here in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 314.316,
          "end": 315.17,
          "en": "And that's of course, similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.17,
          "end": 317.15,
          "en": "to what we do with use selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.15,
          "end": 319.04,
          "en": "Here we also get the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.04,
          "end": 321.36,
          "en": "and drill into the state to get the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.36,
          "end": 324.32,
          "en": "and then store that in a counter const.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.32,
          "end": 326.1,
          "en": "That's basically the equivalent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.1,
          "end": 331.1,
          "en": "when not doing it with hooks, but with the connect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 331.12,
          "end": 333.64,
          "en": "Because now map state to props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.64,
          "end": 336.623,
          "en": "is the first argument we pass to connect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 337.96,
          "end": 340.96,
          "en": "The second argument is another function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.96,
          "end": 344.97,
          "en": "which is typically called map dispatch to props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 344.97,
          "end": 348.08,
          "en": "It's the equivalent to use dispatch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 348.08,
          "end": 352.37,
          "en": "Now the idea is to store dispatch functions in props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 352.37,
          "end": 356.34000000000003,
          "en": "So that in the counter component, we have certain props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 356.34000000000003,
          "end": 359.67,
          "en": "which we can execute as a function, which will then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 359.67,
          "end": 364.373,
          "en": "when executed dispatch an action to the Redux store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 365.88,
          "end": 367.93,
          "en": "For this map dispatch to props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 367.93,
          "end": 372.47,
          "en": "receives the dispatch function as an argument automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 372.47,
          "end": 374.54,
          "en": "just like map states to props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 374.54,
          "end": 376.92,
          "en": "The map dispatch to props function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 376.92,
          "end": 380.42,
          "en": "will be executed for you by Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 380.42,
          "end": 383.79,
          "en": "And then in here, we also return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 383.79,
          "end": 386.37,
          "en": "where the keys are prop names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 386.37,
          "end": 389.07,
          "en": "which we can then use in the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 389.07,
          "end": 392.303,
          "en": "So for example, increment as a name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 393.37,
          "end": 397.32,
          "en": "and the value is then another function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 397.32,
          "end": 402.14,
          "en": "in which we call dispatch and then set up our action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 402.14,
          "end": 403.5,
          "en": "Now, for example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 403.5,
          "end": 405.783,
          "en": "an action where the type is increment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 406.75,
          "end": 409.3,
          "en": "This might look strange, but in the end, this ensures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 409.3,
          "end": 413.39,
          "en": "that in the counter component, we'll have an increment prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 413.39,
          "end": 414.83,
          "en": "which we can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 414.83,
          "end": 417.09000000000003,
          "en": "This prop holds this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 417.09000000000003,
          "end": 418.9,
          "en": "so we can execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 418.9,
          "end": 421.17,
          "en": "from inside the component thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 421.17,
          "end": 424.74,
          "en": "And when we do so, we will call dispatch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 424.74,
          "end": 427.15,
          "en": "and dispatch does action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
